    ('I See Dead People (full)(World Cup 2025)','Djinn''s special rule\nCharacters die as normal but the storytellers doesn’t announce deaths. Dead players can nominate. Poisoned players don’t wake up.\n\nHow to run\nThe main idea of this script is to confuse the town as to whether they are dead or alive. Evil wins by muddying these waters and destroying town''s ability to vote effectively. Town has a set of extremely powerful information gatherers and will win in a vacuum. You can choose to not wake up poisoned players, use this ability aggressively particularly when player numbers get low.\n\nWhen counting votes, make sure to mark player''s who have (perhaps unknowingly) used their dead vote but don''t announce that. Do announce vote totals but do not include in your counts vote from players who are dead and have lost their dead token. If dead players nominate a player run the vote as normal, including players using up ghost vote tokens, but if the person who ends up on the block was nominated by a dead player the execution fails. Do not announce the reason for this- simply \"X player is executed and does not die\".','Ascarywizard'),
    ('Council of the Dead (full)(World Cup 2025)','Djinn Rule: At the start of n4, dead wake together for 2 min, then secretly vote on a living player (if there''s no majority, the ST chooses). The chosen player gets a boon.\n\nOn night 4, all dead players are brought into a private chat for 2 minutes to discuss who they want to give a boon to. Then each dead player privately casts their vote for an alive player. If one player receives a majority, something good happens to them (as chosen by the storytellers). If there is no strict majority, the storytellers decides who receives the boon. The boon given is up to ST discretion, so while it is meant to help, don''t be afraid to balance its strength based on which team is winning.','Ember'),
    ('One Day More (full)(World Cup 2025)','2025 World Cup Script\n\nSpecial rule: Signal Failure: There is a 24 hour delay impacting all characters with abilities that know or learn information.\n\nNotes: - Information is backwards looking to when the ability was used. For example, a Fortune Teller whose picks on night 2 include the Mutant, learns a ''No'' on night 3 even if the Mutant has subsequently been Fang Gu jumped to. - Droisoning only affects the receiving of information. For example, a Sage who dies droisoned on night 3 still learns sober information on night 4, but a Sage who dies sober on night 3 and is droisoned on night 4 receives misinformation. Note: This means that if a Nightwatchman is droisoned the night after they use their ability, a player can learn the wrong person is the Nightwatchman. - The Djinn only affects character abilities containing \"know\" or \"learn\". It does not affect the evil team learning each other or the demon learning bluffs. The artist is also immune.\n\nVersion 1.0.1: Removed Xaan.','Robe'),
    ('Stowed Away (full)(World Cup 2025)','--- CUSTOM DJINN RULE ---\nUp to 2 recommended travellers might be in the bag & the player count lowers accordingly. Travellers are not announced, executions & exiles are equivalent.\n\n--- HOW TO RUN ---\nSetup\nThe General Rule: When racking the game for n players, you can rack any of the following:\n- A standard n player game\n- A standard n-1 player game with one traveller in the bag\n- A standard n-2 player game with two travellers in the bag\n\nSome Examples:\nFor a 12 player game, you can rack\n- 7 Townsfolk, 2 Outsiders, 2 Minions, 1 Demon\n- 7 Townsfolk 1 Outsider, 2 Minions, 1 Demon, 1 Traveller\n- 7 Townsfolk, 0 Outsiders, 2 Minions, 1 Demon, 2 Travellers\nFor a 14 player game, you can rack\n- 9 Townsfolk, 1 Outsider, 3 Minions, 1 Demon\n- 9 Townsfolk, 0 Outsiders, 3 Minions, 1 Demon, 1 Traveller\n- 7 Townsfolk, 2 Outsiders, 2 Minions, 1 Demon, 2 Travellers\nNote that for the 12 players & 2 travellers game, instead of just removing an outsider we are instead dropping from the 13p setup to the 12p setup.\n\nPlease only use the recommended travellers, these can be found in the json and on the night sheet of the pdf.\n\nWhile the travellers you put in the bag must be random as per the rules, it is intended for the alignments of said travellers to be used as a method of counteracting swingy setups. Set their alignment as you please, I trust you to be reasonable.\n\nYou may give Travellers to the Demon as bluffs, please keep in mind the expected Outsider + Traveller count when you do so. If you''re running a 12p game for example, then Outsiders + Travellers = 2, so you should only give Traveller as a bluff if you''d give Outsider as a bluff.\n\nHow to Treat Travellers in the Game\n- You cannot exile players who drew a traveller from the bag, you can only execute them. This executing a traveller successfully will NOT let you execute anyone else like exiling a traveller would.\n- Travellers count towards the player count after the setup. That is unlike a regular game, if there''s a traveller in final 3 or two travellers in final 4, it does not count as reaching the \"two players alive, one of them the demon\" wincon for evil.\n\nSpecific Characters\nTravellers cannot be substituted for any ability that explicitly mentions Townsfolk, Outsider, Minion, or Demon.\nRAI, the Cerenovus can make players mad as travellers (RAW they technically shouldn''t because Travellers aren''t considered to be \"good characters\")\nPoppygrowers explicitly only affect minions/demons, so the travellers can learn their demon.\n\n--- DESCRIPTION ---\nThis is my script submission for the Garden of Djinn Script World Cup competition. There are some travellers in BotC that I''ve always thought would work as standalone characters for either team. Bone Collector is a balanced character for either team, Scapegoat can serve as a hidden extra life for when town makes a mistake or be used to bluff madness breaks and save evil players, Deviant can serve as a method to rule oneself out as a demon candidate and serves as a flexible bluff for DA, and the Apprentice gives you a 2nd copy of some incredibly powerful townsfolk or just straight up removing a detrimental character at the cost of giving evil more claimspace or doubling up on louder minions.\n\nThis being v1.0.0 of a world cup script, expect changes! It''s volatile and I can already think of a few things I want to explore in this space that didn''t come to mind when I originally submitted this.\n(Future Caffeine here, we''re on v2.0.0 now which I expect to be much more stable. Might switch about to add Librarian back in later, but we''ll see how it goes first)\n\nThis entry on the database serves primarily as a resource for player to print and play this irl. To play this script online, please use the version already on the app which has an in-built method to put travellers in the bag.\n\nEnjoy!','CaffeineBoost'),
    ('Djinn''s Bargain (full)(World Cup 2025)','Custom Rule\nNominators may choose to die after making a nomination. If they do, their nominee''s ability works twice until dusk tomorrow.\n\nDescription\nThis script explores the lure of power and the sacrifices required to obtain it. Inspired by the legendary tales of djinns, players face a central mechanic where nominators may choose to forfeit their life after nominating, granting the nominee the ability to use their power twice before dusk on the following day. This trade-off forces players to weigh the benefits of empowering allies against the cost of their own life.\n\nThe script emphasizes themes of ambition, hubris, and the ripple effects of sacrifice. It’s designed to create high-stakes decisions, collaboration, and moments of tension as players attempt to outmaneuver the djinn’s influence. Can the town unite to outsmart the Demon, or will the allure of power tear them apart?\n\nInterview w/ Beardy\n\nHow to Run\nDuring the nomination phase, players may choose to sacrifice themselves to the Djinn when making a nomination. If they do, they immediately die, and the Storyteller announces that they have been sacrificed to the Djinn. The nominee''s ability then works twice until dusk the following day. The onus of sacrificing is on the player, the Storyteller should not prompt or ask if they want to. If they do not announce the sacrifice when nominating someone, their opportunity to sacrifice themselves has passed.\n\nIt is important to note that players cannot sacrifice themselves to the Djinn if only 3 players are alive. This restriction ensures the game remains balanced in its final stages. In such cases, the Storyteller may announce thematically, \"The Djinn has grown weary of sacrifices and will no longer accept them,\" or use something similar to fit the tone of the game. However, this limitation is not included in the official rule text due to naming restrictions for the competition. It may be added to the official text after the tournament is complete.\n\nFurthermore, any ability that causes a player to die upon making a nomination takes priority over sacrificing to the Djinn. For example, Witch-cursed players cannot sacrifice themselves, they die immediately to the Witch, and the Storyteller does not mention the Djinn, so players know the sacrifice was not successful.\n\nFAQs\n\n\nIf I am a \"You Start Knowing\" character do I learn something new the night after I get buffed?\nNo. \"You Start Knowing\" characters only learn information on their first night in the game. However, if a situation ever arises where a \"You Start Knowing\" character enters the game after the overall first night has already occurred and receives a buff on the day before their first night, they will learn two pieces of information that night.\n\n\n\nIf I have a once per game ability, do I get to use it again if I already used it?\nNo. If you have already used your once-per-game ability, you cannot use it again, even if you receive a buff. However, if you have not used your once-per-game ability and then receive a buff, you will be able to use it twice.\n\n\n\nHow does it work if I have a ability that''s triggered by something?\nIf you are buffed and your ability is triggered, it goes into effect twice. For example:\n\nA buffed Ravenkeeper who dies at night would choose two people.\nA buffed Klutz who dies would choose two people.\nA buffed Sweetheart who dies would affect two people.\nA buffed Politician''s alignment swap only happens the first time the ability triggers. Once you swap, you join the winning team. Since your team won, you no longer meet the condition of being \"most responsible for your team losing,\" so you can''t swap back.\n\n\nIf my ability makes me choose multiple people do I choose them all at once?\nNo. In the case of a player choosing multiple people, each choice should be resolved individually, in characterOrder. For example, a buffed Dreamer would choose one player, and the Storyteller would provide them with information on that player. Then, the Storyteller should prompt the Dreamer to choose again.\n\n\n\nDoes a buffed Politician win twice?\nNo. As mentioned previously each instance of a buffed ability should be resolved indiviudally. If a Politician turns evil then they are now on the winning team. As such, when their ability triggers again it is impossible for them to be responsible for their now winning team to lose so they do not switch back.\n\n\n\nDoes a buffed Mayor bounce/win twice?\nNo. Please don''t do this.\n\nNotes\nHere are some interesting interactions that can occur on this script with this custom rule worth noting as well as my own thoughts on why I chose the characters I did.\n\nTownsfolk\nChef/Investigator/Librarian:\nIn a normal game, YSKs provide valuable initial information for the good team but may feel a bit lackluster afterward. The custom rule in this script allows them to take a more active role in their team''s success by strategically sacrificing themselves, enabling others to use their abilities more effectively. Additionally, the Librarian can potentially help solve for the Outsider count. From a Storyteller''s perspective, I also love the idea of showing the Drunk who thinks they are the Librarian a Drunk between two other people.\n\nDreamer:\nSimilar to the Fortune Teller, a buffed Dreamer provides excellent information. It can help identify evil players quickly or confirm good players to build trust chains.\n\nFortune Teller:\nA buffed Fortune Teller is incredibly strong. Given the power the evil team can amass on this script, it’s a great role for the good team to buff in characterOrder to find the Demon as quickly as possible.\n\nOracle:\nThis role enables the good team to potentially determine when evil players sacrificed themselves during the day.\n\nInnkeeper:\nProtecting 4 players at night is incredibly strong, but 2 of them will end up drunk. It’s a trade-off between protection and misinformation.\n\nExorcist:\nSimilar to the Preacher, there are some deadly Demon combos on this script. The Exorcist is a powerful tool against them, especially if buffed and able to identify the Demon.\n\nSeamstress:\nA great role that adds some alignment checking capabilities for the good team. They also have the choice of using their ability and becoming a sacrificial lamb or trying to be greedy and get someone to buff them.\n\nSlayer:\nThis is a powerful role for good that grants them a way to potentially win the game if they can snipe the Demon. It also helps balance the amount of cover and escapes paths the Demon has on this script, especially considering the Djinn rule.\n\nFisherman:\nI always like including at least one once-per-game Townsfolk on a script, and I think the Fisherman fits well here. They can either use their ability early to get advice and then become a sacrificial lamb for the good team, or wait to find someone willing to sacrifice themselves so they can gather double advice on the same day.\n\nRavenkeeper:\nThis is an interesting dynamic because it will always linger in the back of the evil team''s mind. Any buffed good player is an obvious target, but with the Ravenkeeper on the script, the evil team must be cautious about making hasty decisions. Are they the Ravenkeeper? Do I risk it and, if I’m wrong, let them learn two players tonight?\n\nMayor:\nAnother role that grants good another win condition as well as grants the Storyteller some agency via bounced kills.\n\n\n\nOutsiders\nDrunk:\nI personally love the Drunk, but it’s even more detrimental here. If they convince someone to sacrifice themselves, it’s essentially a death for nothing. Figuring out whether you’re the Drunk has never been more important!\n\nPlague Doctor:\nThe Plague Doctor can be devastating for the good team if they die. It grants the Storyteller some agency upon death to grant the evil team a little boost should they need it.\n\nHatter:\nTown will need to be wary of both Demon and, by extension, information manipulation changes. (Optional Hatter rule can be used at ST discrection)\n\nPolitician:\nPolitician: The Politician synergizes extremely well with the custom Djinn rule by granting them an additional avenue through which they can potentially trigger their ability. If you can survive until the end then sacrifice yourself to the Demon to give the evil team that extra boost they need to win!\n\n\n\nMinions\nWitch:\nA fantastic tool for the evil team to deny good players the chance to buff their teammates, as a cursed player would die immediately after nominating, preventing them from sacrificing themselves. Identifying players likely to be one of the roles designed as sacrificial lambs on this script can be highly effective in shutting down the good team''s efforts to buff their abilities.\n\nAssassin:\nA buffed Assassin is extremely powerful on this script. When coordinated well with their fellow evil team, they can effectively obfuscate the reasons for night deaths. Additionally, once their power is used, they can become a sacrificial lamb for their team.\n\nScarlet Woman:\nThe Scarlet Woman is a fantastic backup plan if the Demon gets themselves into trouble. It also synergizes very well with the custom Djinn rule enabling any Demon to now \"Djinnpass\" during the day.\n\nBaron:\nA great Minion that can obscure outsider count, cause havoc and sacrifice themselves willing right from the start.\n\n\n\nDemons\nNo Dashii:\nAnother source of poisoning for evil. Beyond that, it’s essentially just a double kill if buffed.\n\nImp:\nA quintessential Demon for any script. It kills simply and can star pass at night if they need to get out of Dodge.\n\nVortox:\nPrevious iterations of the script had ways for evil to obscure information through poisoning, but they were removed due to bad interactions and syngergy issues. The Vortox maintains that obfuscation of info in some capacity while also adding a win condition for evil.\n\n\n\nTravellers\nButcher:\nThe ability to nominate and buff one more person after the first execution could give either team a significant edge or set them up for a counterplay going into the night phase.\n\nBone Collector:\nA well-timed use of the Bone Collector''s ability could be pivotal in granting either team an additional use of a valuable power.\n\nJudge:\nA well-timed Judge execution could be pivotal in preventing either team from gaining too much power.\n\nApprentice:\nDepending on the ability gained, they can become either a sacrificial lamb for their team or a target to be buffed.\n\nScapegoat:\nThis can be a useful tool for a Storyteller to balance the game if needed, or to add confusion and make things more interesting.\n\nSpecial Thanks\nShoutouts to alasam, Chilip, etonio, reed, thejellydude and zyrain for helping me develop this idea. Appreciate it guys!','phillyCHEEEEEZ'),
    ('The River Styx (full)(World Cup 2025)','World Cup 2025 Garden of Djinn entry.\n\nBootlegger rule: The Ferryman''s ability is amended to: Each night* the demon may choose if all dead players regain their vote token.\n\nThis script contains reasons for minions to play freely as outed evil if caught, knowing that they can make extra plays from the grave! Good players can counter with their own dead votes, but use too many and the Demon may not restore the votes!\n\nv1.2 Updates:\n- Undertaker, + Magician\n\nUndertaker proved to be very strong and confirmable without a grim-peeker on script. I''m bringing back the Magician as it adds a neat puzzle to work through - the Ojo/Vigor have ways around it but both come with tradeoffs that allow the role to still have a beneficial impact for the good team.\n\n-Damsel, +Barber, +Spirit of Ivory\n\nI wanted to add a form of mobility to help out the more immobile demons, especially the Ojo which is on the weaker side compared to the other two demons on script. It also means the evil team can swap in more useful minions like the Scarlet Woman or Poisoner if they are killed early, and have the more expendable ones such as the Baron utilize the Djinn rule from the grave.\n\nSpirit of Ivory has been added to avoid the Mezepheles turning a second player evil in the event of a Barber swap.','Rhea'),
    ('Show Me Wonders (full)(World Cup 2025)',NULL,'DinosaurSatan'),
    ('Buyer''s Remorse (full)(World Cup 2025)','Custom Djinn Rule\nPlayers have 7 gold. Each day, an ability is auctioned, highest unique bidder gains it until dawn, even if dead. Bids are secret & not returned (bar evil ties).\n\nDescription\nA humble merchant has come to peddle their wares at the very same time an evil Demon haunts your village. Can capitalism save these townsfolk? Or will they succumb to the foibles of greed?\n\nLots of fun, either, you start knowing, or once per game roles, that typically, on their own, would not be enough to solve the game. However, with the opportunity to continue accruing abilities, could they be enough to figure out how to kill the Demon?\n\nSpreadsheet for Tracking Bids\nWant to run a game of Buyer''s Remorse but worried about keeping track of the gold? Use this handy dandy spreadsheet that''ll do the work for you!\n\nSteps: 1) Open the link, it''ll automatically ask you to create your own copy of the sheet. 2) On the first page, enter the names of your players in the characterOrder they are sat. 3) Once tokens are passed out, check the boxes for your evil team. 4) Enter the bids as they come in onto the sheet. Use the row that says \"Ability X\" to mark what ability you''re giving out.\n\nThe sheet will automatically flag who won the item (IN GREEN), using the highest unique rule. It''ll also flag any evil player who tied (IN RED) so you can let them know they got their gold back, using the (bar evil ties) rule. The sheet keeps track of everyone''s balance for you and lets you know when they run out of gold (IN GREY). Once you''re done with the game, feel free to use the next tab \"Game 2\" and \"Game 3\" for your next games, or just clear out the bets! It''s that simple.\n\nEnjoy!\n\np.s. if the evil team changes (snake charms, auctioned off mez/ogre, some other ability), just add the player''s name into the bottom table on the day they became evil. This will start keeping track of when you need to return their gold for when they tie. p.p.s. thank you megan (vanillascrewdriver) for making this for me i love you forever\n\nhttps://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1vpP2axBqED9u84ayaYHniaJEeTW_ywOmeQe_0d2b05E/copy\n\nFrequently Asked Questions\n1) Format is completely up to the ST for how auctions should be run. I''ve done top of the day, announce the item, take bids throughout the day, then let the winner know secretly prior to nominations. I''ve seen before nominations the item is announced so no private chat about the actual ability occurs. As long as an auction starts and ends once per day, that''s satisfying the Djinn.\n\n2) Lots of questions can be answered with \"The ability comes from the Djinn.\" The Djinn cannot be drunk or poisoned so the ability is considered sober at all times, even if the player becomes drunk or poisoned. Additionally, they can be executed or die that night, but still use the Djinn granted ability.\n\n3) Players cannot share gold nor can they bid in smaller increments than 1 gold. .5 gold is NOT allowed!\n\n4) The ability does not necessarily need to be on-script. All the Djinn says is \"an ability\", go wild!\n\n5) Abilities can persist past the dawn, but they are no longer possessed by that player that won it. If you auction the Sweetheart ability, and that player dies that night, a player does stay drunk for the rest of the game. If you auction a Witch ability, the player cursed by the Witch will still die if they nominate. If you auction an Artist ability, that player must use it before the night phase, or they lose their chance.\n\n6) Djinn granted abilities do not change a player''s token. So if you auction a Snake Charmer ability and the Chef wins it and they pick the Imp, the Imp becomes a poisoned, good Chef and the previous Chef becomes an evil Imp. If the Dreamer were to pick the Chef who won the Snake Charmer ability, the good ability they''d see is the Chef token. The ability won from the auction is provided by the Djinn from the moment they win it to the next dawn. The Djinn grants the ability to any player that wins it, no matter if they are drunk, poisoned, or dead. Gold cannot be split, exchanged, or shared. The only time a player can receive their gold back is if they are evil and they bid the same amount as another player.\n\n7) Grim Peekers should only be able to see established reminder tokens that would be on a Clocktower Grim. If you want to use reminder tokens to keep track of the Gold, you should not have those in view for any Grim Peekers.\n\n8) How does the highest, unique bidding work and (bar evil ties)?\n\nGood player 1 submits 7 gold Good player 2 submits 7 gold Evil player 1 submits 7 gold -- Good player 3 submits 6 gold -- Good player 4 submits 5 gold Evil player 2 submits 5 gold -- Evil player 3 submits 4 gold\n\nGood players 1, 2, 3, 4 all lose the gold they bid Evil players 1, 2 get their gold back (they tied) Evil player 3 loses their gold Good player 3 wins the item as they were the highest, unique bid.','mist'),
    ('bag-duplicate (full)(World Cup 2025)','Djinn rule: All minions are Witches. Nominated demons cannot move tonight.\n\n(script JSON now supports putting duplicate Witches in the bag','Nick B'),
    ('Binary Supernovae (full)(World Cup 2025)','Djinnlegger Rule: If a Demon dies by execution, good wins. Summoner only removes 1 Demon. [+1 Demon]\n\nBinary Supernovae is a Garden of Djinn World Cup finalist script featuring not one, but 2 demons! They''ll have to work together to wipe out the good team as efficiently as possible, but the catch is that good only needs to find one of them. Each demon has their own strengths and weaknesses to play around, and who knows, maybe they''ll even kill each other! Will the good team find a demon before it''s too late?\n\nFeel free to reach out to me with any & all questions and feedback!! I''m trying to do everything I can to make this script shine, and your input matters to me. You can find me on discord @Hystrex, I''m on the unofficial server a lot (.gg/botc) and occasionally a few other places.\n\nCheck out this script''s website!! https://beardytas.com/garden-of-djinn/binary-supernovae/\n\nHow to Run: When creating the bag, remove a Townsfolk token and replace it with a Demon token. On the first night, wake the Demons together to learn who the Minions are, much like how Minions wake together to learn the Demon normally. Each Demon gets their own set of bluffs, which may or may not overlap. If any Demon dies by execution, immediately end the game and announce that the good team has won, unless an ability says otherwise (i.e. Mastermind). If a Minion dies, or a Demon dies to an ability, this does not happen (including if a Summoner dies before creating a Demon).\n\nClarifications: 1. The Djinnlegger rule removes a Townsfolk, not a Minion (or Outsider). A valid character distribution might look like 6 Townsfolk / 2 Outsiders / 2 Minions / 2 Demons. 2. Summoner’s setup text is amended to [-1 Demon]. Nothing else is changed about it. 3. This means that Summoner can duplicate an in-play Demon. I’m perfectly fine with STs allowing this, or not, just be clear before the game starts. 4. Good should win at the end of a Mastermind day unless a good player is executed, in which case evil wins. This is not the only valid interpretation, but it’s my preferred ruling. 5. In the same vein, if the Imp starpasses to the Mastermind on a Mastermind day, the game continues as normal (because there’s no more Mastermind ability and neither team is meeting a win condition).\n\nST Recommendations: 1. Include a mix of decelerators and ongoing info if you can help it. 2. Don’t be afraid to remove an outsider with Godfather. The outsiders are intentionally potent bluffs, so -1 can be stronger than +1 at times. 3. Let days be longer than they normally would be. There’s about twice the number of kills each night, so there are fewer days. 4. Don’t use an Ojo miss to kill more than one player, evil doesn’t need the help. DEFINITELY don’t do that to hide a Mastermind day. 5. Alternative ruling: some STs like to run this script where the Demons don’t natively learn each other. If you think you’d prefer this, feel free to run it this way! Obviously tell your players in advance. This has been dubbed the “Luis Rule”.\n\nI plan to keep this updated as the World Cup goes on. Good luck to the other 15!','Hystrex'),
    ('The Warrens (full)(World Cup 2025)','==Djinn Rule==\n\nIf 5 or more players live, evil players who nominate other living evil players (not Travellers) immediately swap charactes\n\n==How to Run==\n\nIf an evil player nominates another living evil player while 5 or more players live, immediately swap their character tokens. When the game enters the night phase, inform the two players of their new roles. Travellers are unaffected.\n\n==Tricky Interactions==\n\nPreacher - A ‘preached’ Minion becomes unpreached if they swap with the Demon. The ‘preached’ condition is removed completely if this happens.\n\nExample: Dan is the Cerenovus. He is preached & loses his ability. He nominates the Demon, becoming the No Dashii. He then nominates another Minion, becoming the Assassin. As the Assassin, he is not affected by the Preacher and has his ability.\n\nA ‘preached’ Minion does not become unpreached if they nominate-swap with another Minion.\n\nExample: Zylus is the Cerenovus. He is preached, and loses his ability. He nominates Amy the Widow, swapping characters. He is now a ‘preached’ Widow and still has no ability. Amy, however, is now a functioning Cerenovus.\n\nGoblin - A Goblin’s ability can only trigger if they claim to be the Goblin while they are actually the Goblin.\n\nExample: Lachlan is the Kazali. He is nominated, and claims to be the Goblin. He gets 8 votes. He then nominates Ben the Goblin, becoming the new Goblin. Lachlan’s execution will not trigger the Goblin win condition.\n\nWidow - A swapped Widow picks a new target that night. A new good player is not notified that a Widow is in play.\n\nNo Dashii - A swapped No Dashii immediately poisons its new Townsfolk neighbours\n\nAssassin - A swapped Assassin gains a new instance of its ability\n\n==Other Notes==\n\nThis is version three of the World Cup script, with a number of changes made.','Zets'),
    ('Trained Killer (full)(World Cup 2025)','TPI 2025 Garden of Djinn World Cup Top 8 Script.\n\nDjinn rule: Each night*, the Demon attacks the next living in-play character(s) in script characterOrder. Characters who survive might get reattacked.\n\nThis script determines a kill characterOrder for the two Demons who normally kill via the ST. It is intentionally out of SAO and the characterOrder is carefully constructed to work with the Djinn rule. Demon works down the list but might retarget players who survive.\n\nBelow info also here, looking nicer: https://beardytas.com/trained-killer/\n\nHow to run:\n\nStarting from Night 2:\n- If the Demon is Yaggababble, determine the number of kills based on the repetition of their phrase as usual. If Lil'' Monsta, generally stick to a single kill.\n- Find the next living in-play character(s) on the grim, starting from the top of the script with Mayor, matching the number of kills.\n- The Demon will attack these characters tonight. For example, if there is no Mayor, but there is a single Village Idiot and an Artist, and Yaggababble said their phrase twice, these two will be targeted.\n- Check if any abilities affected kills. Mayor, Lycanthrope, Monk, Amnesiac, and Spy could all disrupt the Demon''s kill pattern. - Announce the kills in the morning accordingly.\n- In subsequent nights, if any characters survived the attack, they might be attacked again, or get skipped, Storyteller''s choice. For example, if the Mayor bounced on Night 2, they could be targeted again on Night 3, dying now, or the Demon can move on down the script to the next target(s).\n\nFAQ: Day kills: RAI, Yaggababble and Harpy are allowed to simulate each other, but a strict reading of the Djinn rule RAW might mean Yaggababble is only allowed to kill at night, so feel free to adjust Harpy kills accordingly. A more generous reading of the Djinn rule is that it doesn''t say anything about day kills, and therefore Yaggababble can anyone kill during the day as usual. It is up to the ST to determine which reading they''ll go for. Author believes in the flexibility and therefore prefers a more generous reading but understands if other STs prefer the strict version.\n\nGoing back up top for reattacking: Here''s a neat summary, courtesy of oddGarrett,\n\n\"I see three ways of running Trained Killer, and I''m not sure which I prefer (probably not option 3)\n\nEach night* attack the first never-targeted character on the script, or the player who survived an attack last night. (i.e. if you don''t re-attack a player the following night, they never get targeted again)\n\nEach night* attack the first never-targeted character on the script, or ANY player who has survived an attack. (i.e. jump back up the script for one night, but resume from the furthest place you''ve got to)\n\nEach night* attack the first character on the script below last night''s target, or any player who has survived an attack (i.e. a Storyteller can \"jump back up\" but then restarts attacking from that point in the script characterOrder)\"\n\nVillage Idiot targeting: Targeting one Village Idiot satisfies the Djinn rule. The remaining Idiots would survive, and can get reattacked in subsequent nights, or get skipped. If Yaggababble has said their phrase multiple times, you can target multiple Idiots all at once, or target one and move on down the list, Storyteller''s choice.\n\nLycanthrope and Demon kills: The Demon still attacks the next target even if the Lycanthrope killed a good player successfully. Demons who pick their kill are still woken to choose a target even if a Lycanthrope kills, so the same principle applies here. Therefore, \"the cursor still moves\", i.e. the Demon does not get stuck on the same target because the Lycanthrope keeps killing good players.','Ekin'),
    ('The Phantom Detectives (full)(World Cup 2025)','Dead players (not Demons) keep their abilities. Each Townsfolk loses their ability at the start of night 1, then regains it on death.\n\nTownsfolk who die become powerful ghosts who commune with the living to solve their own murder. The evil team may keep dangerous Townsfolk alive to deny them info, and good characters will be angling to get killed at a critical moment.\n\nHow to run\nAt the beginning of the first night phase, all Townsfolk lose their abilities, and do not wake to make choices or learn information.\nTownsfolk setup effects still happen, as they occurred before the game began.\nWhen players die for any reason, they lose their ability only if they were a Demon: continue to wake Outsiders & Minions like living players.\nWhen a Townsfolk dies, they immediately regain their ability, and will have it for the rest of the game, acting at their designated spot in the night characterOrder if applicable.\nTownsfolk who act on a certain trigger (e.g. \"When you die at night\") act immediately if they died the correct way.\n\"You start knowing\" Townsfolk act after the Demon on the first night that they are dead.\nHow to run - by character\nCult Leader\nWhat happens to the Cult Leader when only evil players are alive?\n\nIf the last good player dies and there is no route to victory for the good team, the game should immediately end without resolving any further player abilities. This means the Cult Leader, if good, does not get to switch alignment one last time and win with the evil team.\n\nHatter\nShould I use the Hatter''s optional rule?\n\nNo!\n\nI strongly encourage running the \"standard\" Hatter when playing this script: i.e. Demons must choose Demon characters and Minions must choose Minion characters. A Demon who is desperate to escape from a tight spot can always choose to become an Imp when the Hatter dies.\n\nScarlet Woman\nDoes a dead Scarlet Woman block an Imp from star-passing?\n\nUpdate, V4: No! The Imp''s almanac reads \"if the Imp kills themself at night, they die and an alive Minion becomes an Imp.\" This means that (for example) if the Scarlet Woman is dead, but the Boffin is alive, the Imp-hood must pass to the Boffin.\n\nI am aware that the Scarlet Woman''s almanac says \"the Scarlet Woman must become the new Imp.\" Rules-as-written, this means you should also turn the dead Scarlet Woman into a dead Imp. However, dead Demons do not have an ability on The Phantom Detectives, so this makes no mechanical difference to the game: the Scarlet Woman becomes a dead Imp and does nothing.\n\nBoffin\nDo Demons get to use the Boffin ability while they’re alive?\n\nYes! And if you’re playing online, it might be a good idea to remind the Demon of the Djinn’s special rule before they go telling people that they’re the High Priestess and were told to speak to them. The Boffin lets a Demon secretly gather information while they’re alive, or might give them a fun effect on death: Plague Doctor, Hatter and Farmer are all great Boffin abilities for a Demon who might die at night. The Boffin ability can also (and probably should) change when a new Demon is created.\n\nDo Demons get to use the Boffin ability while they’re dead?\n\nMaybe! Exactly 1 Demon may have a Boffin ability at a time. The dead Demon may keep their ability or the living Demon may gain a new one. Here''s how I''d rule it...\n\nAs per the almanac, if the Boffin ability is an effect that only persists while the user is dead, the first Demon must keep its Boffin ability and the new Demon may not gain a new one. (Relevant abilities: Banshee, Sweetheart.)\nIf the Boffin ability is an effect that is triggered on death but has an effect that does not require the character to remain in play, that ability triggers, and then the new Demon may gain a new ability. (Relevant abilities: Farmer, Plague Doctor, Hatter.)\nFor all other Boffin abilities, I would argue that you should do whatever you think will make the game more fun.\nIf you think the newly-executed Ojo will struggle to keep up their Dreamer bluff, you can leave the Dreamer ability with the dead Ojo and accept that this means the Scarlet Woman-turned-Ojo gets nothing. If you think it''s better for the evil team that the new Demon gets a new Boffin ability, you can do that instead. It''s up to you.\n\nChanges from v3\nWe get to make six changes between World Cup matches. Here''s what''s changed compared to version 3:\n\nEngineer → Amnesiac\nKazali added\nThe Amnesiac is on the case! A fun thing on this script is that the Amnesiac (and therefore, also, the Storyteller) can estimate how long they have to work out their ability. If you wake up dead with 5 players alive, you have 2 days to work it out! The Djinn rule also makes it easier to run Amnesiac abilities that interact with other characters. On other scripts, an Amnesiac who learns something about the High Priestess''s information will stop waking when the High Priestess does, but here, you know the High Priestess will stick around.\n\nThe Kazali is a fun fourth Demon as all four Minions have interesting synergies with each other. Boomdandy and Organ Grinder pair particularly well together, and Scarlet Woman and Boffin do too. It''s also the only evil character capable of increasing the Outsider count (outside of a Balloonist Boffin).','Schnauzer '),
    ('The Ballad of Seat 7 (full)(World Cup 2025)','Custom Djinn Rule\nSeat 7 remains empty. It''s choices are arbitrary. Once per game the storytellers may speak on it''s behalf.\n\nHow to Run\nSeat 7 runs for the most part like any other Clocktower game. One seat remains open and tokens are passed out as usual. Each night the storytellers determines what actions the seat takes following its role in night characterOrder. Once per game the storytellers may choose to speak for the seat. This can be public or private and does not need to be the truth, as an evil seat may want to bluff to help their team win. A storytellers may also choose to not use this ability if they think it will benefit the seat''s team to stay silent. This ability can also be used to nominate and accuse another player.\n\nAdvice on Speaking for the Seat\nA storytellers only has one opportunity to influence the game using the seat''s voice so it is advised to be very careful when you speak and what you say. A seat who speaks on day 1 may have game solving info later. It is also encouraged to get creative with how you choose to use the seat''s voice. The goal is not to save the seat but to win the game for the seat''s team.\n\nKnockout Changes\nChanges were minimal this round to preserve the feeling of the script.\n\nFortune Teller --> Village Idiot Village Idiot was added to give the evil team an easy bluff in the event of a Seat 7 demon game as well as add one more source of night 1 misinformation.','TrashWarlock'),
    ('Nobody Fucking Move (Teensyville)','A very silly script people seem to enjoy. A shoutout goes to members of the Clock On The Bloodtower server who have played this a fair bit & recommended the addition of the Sentinel to help hide the potential of a Heretic being in play.','Brockwell'),
    ('Catfishing - v11.1.0',NULL,'Emily'),
    ('Sound of Madness',NULL,'Bones About It !!!'),
    ('Plus One',NULL,'Dragon Charlz'),
    ('Extension Cord',NULL,'Viva La Sam'),
    ('Teeny Brewing - v1.0.0 (Teensyville)','For begineer ST o_O','Malcolm Ryan'),
    ('Trouble Brewing (base)',NULL,'The Pandemonium Institute'),
    ('Bad Moon Rising (base)',NULL,'The Pandemonium Institute'),
    ('Sects & Violets (base)',NULL,'The Pandemonium Institute');
INSERT INTO `character_` (name, alignment, description, link_to_wiki, max_start_number, tips, image_uploaded) VALUES ('Washerwoman','Townsfolk','You start knowing that 1 of 2 playrs is a particular Townsfolk.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Washerwoman',1,'niebondźglizdom',1),('Librarian','Townsfolk','You start knowing that 1 of 2 playrs is a particular Outsider, or that zero are in play.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Librarian',1,null,1),('Investigator','Townsfolk','You start knowing that 1 of 2 playrs is playrs particular Minion.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Investigator',1,null,1),('Chef','Townsfolk','You start knowing how many pairs of evil players there are.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Chef',1,null,1),('Empath','Townsfolk','Each night, you learn how many of your 2 alive neighbors are evil.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Empath',1,null,1),('Fortune Teller','Townsfolk','Each night, choose 2 playrs: you learn if either is a Demon. There is a good player that always registers as a Demon to you.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Fortune_Teller',1,null,1),('Undertaker','Townsfolk','Each night*, you learn which character died by execution today.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Undertaker',1,null,1),('Monk','Townsfolk','Each night*, choose a player (not yourself): they are safe from the Demon tonight.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Monk',1,null,1),('Ravenkeeper','Townsfolk','If you die at night, you are woken to choose a player: you learn their character.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Ravenkeeper',1,null,1),('Virgin','Townsfolk','The first time you are nominated, if the nominator is a Townsfolk, they are executed immediately.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Virgin',1,null,1),('Slayer','Townsfolk','Once per game, during the day, publicly choose a player: if they are the Demon, they die.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Slayer',1,null,1),('Soldier','Townsfolk','You are safe from the Demon.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Soldier',1,null,1),('Mayor','Townsfolk','If only 3 playrs live & no execution occurs, your team wins. If you die at night, another player might die instead.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Mayor',1,null,1),('Butler','Outsider','Each night, choose a player (not yourself): tomorrow, you may only vote if they are voting too.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Butler',1,null,1),('Drunk','Outsider','You do not know you are the Drunk. You think you are a Townsfolk character, but you are not.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Drunk',1,null,1),('Recluse','Outsider','You might register as evil & as a Minion or Demon, even if dead.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Recluse',1,null,1),('Saint','Outsider','If you die by execution, your team loses.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Saint',1,null,1),('Poisoner','Minion','Each night, choose a player: they are poisoned tonight and tomorrow day.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Poisoner',1,null,1),('Spy','Minion','Each night, you see the Grimoire. You might register as good & as a Townsfolk or Outsider, even if dead.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Spy',1,null,1),('Baron','Minion','There are 2 extra Outsiders in play.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Baron',1,null,1),('Scarlet Woman','Minion','If there are 5 or more players alive & the Demon dies, you become the Demon. (Travellers don''t count)','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Scarlet_Woman',1,null,1),('Imp','Demon','Each night*, choose a player: they die. If you kill yourself this way, a Minion becomes the Imp.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Imp',1,null,1),('Grandmother','Townsfolk','You start knowing a good player & their character. If the Demon kills them, you die too.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Grandmother',1,null,1),('Sailor','Townsfolk','Each night, choose an alive player: either you or they are drunk until dusk. You can''t die.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Sailor',1,null,1),('Chambermaid','Townsfolk','Each night, choose 2 alive players (not yourself): you learn how many woke tonight  due to their ability.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Chambermaid',1,null,1),('Exorcist','Townsfolk','Each night*, choose a player (different to last night): the Demon, if chosen, learns who you are then doesn''t wake tonight','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Exorcist',1,null,1),('Innkeeper','Townsfolk','Each night*, choose 2 players: they can''t die tonight, but 1 is drunk until dusk.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Innkeeper',1,null,1),('Gambler','Townsfolk','Each night*, choose a player & guess their character: if you guess wrong, you die.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Gambler',1,null,1),('Gossip','Townsfolk','Each day, you may make a public statement. Tonight, if it was true, a player dies.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Gossip',1,null,1),('Courtier','Townsfolk','Once per game, at night, choose a character: they are drunk for 3 nights & 3 days.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Courtier',1,null,1),('Professor','Townsfolk','Once per game, at night*, choose a dead player: if they are a Townsfolk, they are resurrected.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Professor',1,null,1),('Minstrel','Townsfolk','When a Minion dies by execution, all other players (except Travellers) are drunk until dusk tomorrow.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Minstrel',1,null,1),('Tea Lady','Townsfolk','If both your alive neighbors are good, they can''t die.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Tea_Lady',1,null,1),('Pacifist','Townsfolk','Executed good players might not die.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Pacifist',1,null,1),('Fool','Townsfolk','The 1st time you die, you don''t.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Fool',1,null,1),('Goon','Outsider','Each night, the 1st player to choose you with their ability is drunk until dusk. You become their alignment.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Goon',1,null,1),('Lunatic','Outsider','You think you are a Demon, but you are not. The Demon knows who you are & who you choose at night.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Lunatic',1,null,1),('Tinker','Outsider','You might die at any time.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Tinker',1,null,1),('Moonchild','Outsider','When you learn that you died, publicly choose 1 alive player. Tonight, if it was a good player, they die.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Moonchild',1,null,1),('Godfather','Minion','You start knowing which Outsiders are in play. If 1 died today, choose a player tonight: they die. [-1 or +1 Outsider]','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Godfather',1,null,1),('Assassin','Minion','Once per game, at night*, choose a player: they die, even if for some reason they could not.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Assassin',1,null,1),
('Devil''s advocate','Minion','Each night, choose a living player (different to last night): if executed tomorrow, they don''t die.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Devil%27s_Advocate',1,null,1),('Mastermind','Minion','If the Demon dies by execution (ending the game,null), play for 1 more day. If a player is then executed, their team loses.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Mastermind',1,null,1),('Zombuul','Demon','Each night*, if no-one died today, choose a player: they die. The 1st time you die, you live but register as dead.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Zombuul',1,null,1),('Pukka','Demon','Each night, choose a player: they are poisoned. The previously poisoned player dies then becomes healthy.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Pukka',1,null,1),('Shabaloth','Demon','Each night*, choose 2 players: they die. A dead player you chose last night might be regurgitated.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Shabaloth',1,null,1),('Po','Demon','Each night*, you may choose a player: they die. If your last choice was no-one, choose 3 players tonight.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Po',1,null,1),('Clockmaker','Townsfolk','You start knowing how many steps from the Demon to its nearest Minion.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Clockmaker',1,null,1),('Dreamer','Townsfolk','Each night, choose a player (not yourself or Travellers): you learn 1 good & 1 evil character, 1 of which is correct.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Dreamer',1,null,1),('Snake Charmer','Townsfolk','Each night, choose an alive player: a chosen Demon swaps characters & alignments with you & is then poisoned.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Snake_Charmer',1,null,1),('Mathematician','Townsfolk','Each night, you learn how many players'' abilities worked abnormally (since dawn) due to another character''s ability.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Mathematician',1,null,1),('Flowergirl','Townsfolk','Each night*, you learn if a Demon voted today.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Flowergirl',1,null,1),('Town Crier','Townsfolk','Each night*, you learn if a Minion nominated today.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Town_Crier',1,null,1),('Oracle','Townsfolk','Each night*, you learn how many dead players are evil.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Oracle',1,null,1),('Savant','Townsfolk','Each day, you may visit the Storyteller to learn 2 things in private: 1 is true & 1 is false.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Savant',1,null,1),('Seamstress','Townsfolk','Once per game, at night, choose 2 players (not yourself): you learn if they are the same alignment.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Seamstress',1,null,1),('Philosopher','Townsfolk','Once per game, at night, choose a good character: gain that ability. If this character is in play, they are drunk.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Philosopher',1,null,1),('Artist','Townsfolk','Once per game, during the day, privately ask the Storyteller any yes/no question.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Artist',1,null,1),('Juggler','Townsfolk','On your 1st day, publicly guess up to 5 players'' characters. That night, you learn how many you got correct.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Juggler',1,null,1),('Sage','Townsfolk','If the Demon kills you, you learn that it is 1 of 2 players.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Sage',1,null,1),('Mutant','Outsider','If you are \"mad\" about being an Outsider, you might be executed.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Mutant',1,null,1),('Sweetheart','Outsider','When you die, 1 player is drunk from now on.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Sweetheart',1,null,1),('Barber','Outsider','If you died today or tonight, the Demon may choose 2 players (not another Demon) to swap characters.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Barber',1,null,1),('Klutz','Outsider','When you learn that you died, publicly choose 1 alive player: if they are evil, your team loses.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Klutz',1,null,1),('Evil Twin','Minion','You & an opposing player know each other. If the good player is executed, evil wins. Good can''t win if you both live.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Evil_Twin',1,null,1),('Witch','Minion','Each night, choose a player: if they nominate tomorrow, they die. If just 3 players live, you lose this ability.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Witch',1,null,1),('Cerenovus','Minion','Each night, choose a player & a good character: they are \"mad\" they are this character tomorrow, or might be executed.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Cerenovus',1,null,1),('Pit-Hag','Minion','Each night*, choose a player & a character they become (if not in play). If a Demon is made, deaths tonight are arbitrary.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Pit-Hag',1,null,1),('Fang Gu','Demon','Each night*, choose a player: they die. The 1st Outsider this kills becomes an evil Fang Gu & you die instead. [+1 Outsider]','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Fang_Gu',1,null,1),('Vigormortis','Demon','Each night*, choose a player: they die. Minions you kill keep their ability & poison 1 Townsfolk neighbor. [-1 Outsider]','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Vigormortis',1,null,1),('No Dashii','Demon','Each night*, choose a player: they die. Your 2 Townsfolk neighbors are poisoned.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/No_Dashii',1,null,1),('Vortox','Demon','Each night*, choose a player: they die. Townsfolk abilities yield false info. Each day, if no-one is executed, evil wins.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Vortox',1,null,1),('Acrobat','Townsfolk','Each night*, choose a player: if they are or become drunk or poisoned tonight, you die.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Acrobat',1,null,1),('Alchemist','Townsfolk','You have a Minion ability. When using this, the Storyteller may prompt you to choose differently.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Alchemist',1,null,1),('Alsaahir','Townsfolk','Each day, if you publicly guess which players are Minion(s) and which are Demon(s,null), good wins.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Alsaahir',1,null,1),('Amnesiac','Townsfolk','You do not know what your ability is. Each day, privately guess what it is: you learn how accurate you are.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Amnesiac',1,null,1),('Atheist','Townsfolk','The Storyteller can break the game rules, and if executed, good wins, even if you are dead. [No evil characters]','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Atheist',1,null,1),('Balloonist','Townsfolk','Each night, you learn a player of a different character type than last night. [+0 or +1 Outsider]','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Balloonist',1,null,1),
('Banshee','Townsfolk','If the Demon kills you, all players learn this. From now on, you may nominate twice per day and vote twice per nomination.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Banshee',1,null,1),('Bounty Hunter','Townsfolk','You start knowing 1 evil player. If the player you know dies, you learn another evil player tonight. [1 Townsfolk is evil]','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Bounty_Hunter',1,null,1),('Cannibal','Townsfolk','You have the ability of the recently killed executee. If they are evil, you are poisoned until a good player dies by execution.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Cannibal',1,null,1),('Choirboy','Townsfolk','If the Demon kills the King, you learn which player is the Demon. [+the King]','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Choirboy',1,null,1),('Cult Leader','Townsfolk','Each night, you become the alignment of an alive neighbor. If all good players choose to join your cult, your team wins.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Cult_Leader',1,null,1),('Engineer','Townsfolk','Once per game, at night, choose which Minions or which Demon is in play.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Engineer',1,null,1),('Farmer','Townsfolk','When you die at night, an alive good player becomes a Farmer.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Farmer',1,null,1),('Fisherman','Townsfolk','Once per game, during the day, visit the Storyteller for some advice to help your team win.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Fisherman',1,null,1),('General','Townsfolk','Each night, you learn which alignment the Storyteller believes is winning: good, evil, or neither.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/General',1,null,1),('High Priestess','Townsfolk','Each night, learn which player the Storyteller believes you should talk to most.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/High_Priestess',1,null,1),('Huntsman','Townsfolk','Once per game, at night, choose a living player: the Damsel, if chosen, becomes a not-in-play Townsfolk. [+the Damsel]','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Huntsman',1,null,1),('King','Townsfolk','Each night, if the dead equal or outnumber the living, you learn 1 alive character. The Demon knows you are the King.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/King',1,null,1),('Knight','Townsfolk','You start knowing 2 players that are not the Demon.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Knight',1,null,1),('Lycanthrope','Townsfolk','Each night*, choose an alive player. If good, they die & the Demon doesn’t kill tonight. One good player registers as evil.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Lycanthrope',1,null,1),('Magician','Townsfolk','The Demon thinks you are a Minion. Minions think you are a Demon.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Magician',1,null,1),('Nightwatchman','Townsfolk','Once per game, at night, choose a player: they learn you are the Nightwatchman.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Nightwatchman',1,null,1),('Noble','Townsfolk','You start knowing 3 players, 1 and only 1 of which is evil.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Noble',1,null,1),('Pixie','Townsfolk','You start knowing 1 in-play Townsfolk. If you were mad that you were this character, you gain their ability when they die.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Pixie',1,null,1),('Poppy Grower','Townsfolk','Minions & Demons do not know each other. If you die, they learn who each other are that night.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Poppy_Grower',1,null,1),('Preacher','Townsfolk','Each night, choose a player: a Minion, if chosen, learns this. All chosen Minions have no ability.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Preacher',1,null,1),('Shugenja','Townsfolk','You start knowing if your closest evil player is clockwise or anti-clockwise. If equidistant, this info is arbitrary.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Shugenja',1,null,1),('Steward','Townsfolk','You start knowing 1 good player.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Steward',1,null,1),('Village Idiot','Townsfolk','Each night, choose a player: you learn their alignment. [+0 to +2 Village Idiots. 1 of the extras is drunk]','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Village_Idiot',3,null,1),('Damsel','Outsider','All Minions know a Damsel is in play. If a Minion publicly guesses you (once,null), your team loses.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Damsel',1,null,1),('Golem','Outsider','You may only nominate once per game. When you do, if the nominee is not the Demon, they die.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Golem',1,null,1),('Hatter','Outsider','If you died today or tonight, the Minion & Demon players may choose new Minion & Demon characters to be.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Hatter',1,null,1),('Heretic','Outsider','Whoever wins, loses & whoever loses, wins, even if you are dead.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Heretic',1,null,1),('Ogre','Outsider','On your 1st night, choose a player (not yourself): you become their alignment (you don''t know which) even if drunk or poisoned.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Ogre',1,null,1),('Plague Doctor','Outsider','When you die, the Storyteller gains a Minion ability.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Plague_Doctor',1,null,1),('Politician','Outsider','If you were the player most responsible for your team losing, you change alignment & win, even if dead.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Politician',1,null,1),('Puzzlemaster','Outsider','1 player is drunk, even if you die. If you guess (once) who it is, learn the Demon player, but guess wrong & get false info.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Puzzlemaster',1,null,1),('Snitch','Outsider','Each Minion gets 3 bluffs.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Snitch',1,null,1),('Zealot','Outsider','If there are 5 or more players alive, you must vote for every nomination.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Zealot',1,null,1),('Boffin','Minion','The Demon (even if drunk or poisoned) has a not-in-play good character''s ability. You both know which.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Boffin',1,null,1),('Boomdandy','Minion','If you are executed, all but 3 players die. After a 10 to 1 countdown, the player with the most players pointing at them, dies.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Boomdandy',1,null,1),('Fearmonger','Minion','Each night, choose a player: if you nominate & execute them, their team loses. All players know if you choose a new player.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Fearmonger',1,null,1),('Goblin','Minion','If you publicly claim to be the Goblin when nominated & are executed that day, your team wins.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Goblin',1,null,1),('Harpy','Minion','Each night, choose 2 players: tomorrow, the 1st player is mad that the 2nd is evil, or one or both might die.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Harpy',1,null,1),
('Marionette','Minion','You think you are a good character, but you are not. The Demon knows who you are. [You neighbor the Demon]','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Marionette',1,null,1),('Mezepheles','Minion','You start knowing a secret word. The 1st good player to say this word becomes evil that night.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Mezepheles',1,null,1),('Organ Grinder','Minion','All players keep their eyes closed when voting and the vote tally is secret. Each night, choose if you are drunk until dusk.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Organ_Grinder',1,null,1),('Psychopath','Minion','Each day, before nominations, you may publicly choose a player: they die. If executed, you only die if you lose roshambo.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Psychopath',1,null,1),('Summoner','Minion','You get 3 bluffs. On the 3rd night, choose a player: they become an evil Demon of your choice. [No Demon]','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Summoner',1,null,1),('Vizier','Minion','All players know you are the Vizier. You cannot die during the day. If good voted, you may choose to execute immediately.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Vizier',1,null,1),('Widow','Minion','On your first night, look at the Grimoire & choose a player: they are poisoned. 1 good player knows a Widow is in play.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Widow',1,null,1),('Wizard','Minion','Once per game, choose to make a wish. If granted, it might have a price & leave a clue as to its nature.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Wizard',1,null,1),('Xaan','Minion','On night X, all Townsfolk are poisoned until dusk. [X Outsiders]','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Xaan',1,null,1),('Al-Hadikhia','Demon','Each night*, you may choose 3 players (all players learn who): each silently chooses to live or die, but if all live, all die.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Al-Hadikhia',1,null,1),('Kazali','Demon','Each night*, choose a player: they die. [You choose which players are which Minions. -? to +? Outsiders]','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Kazali',1,null,1),('Legion','Demon','Each night*, a player might die. Executions fail if only evil voted. You register as a Minion too. [Most players are Legion]','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Legion',10,null,1),('Leviathan','Demon','If more than 1 good player is executed, evil wins. All players know you are in play. After day 5, evil wins.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Leviathan',1,null,1),('Lil Monsta','Demon','Each night, Minions choose who babysits Lil'' Monsta & ''is the Demon''. Each night*, a player might die. [+1 Minion]','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Lil%27_Monsta',1,null,1),('Lleech','Demon','Each night*, choose a player: they die. You start by choosing a player: they are poisoned. You die if & only if they are dead.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Lleech',1,null,1),('Lord of Typhon','Demon','Each night*, choose a player: they die. [Evil characters are in a line. You are in the middle. +1 Minion. -? to +? Outsiders]','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Lord_of_Typhon',1,null,1),('Ojo','Demon','Each night*, choose a character: they die. If they are not in play, the Storyteller chooses who dies.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Ojo',1,null,1),('Riot','Demon','On day 3, Minions become Riot & nominees die but nominate an alive player immediately. This must happen.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Riot',1,null,1),('Yaggababble','Demon','You start knowing a secret phrase. For each time you said it publicly today, a player might die.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Yaggababble',1,null,1),('Scapegoat','Traveller','If a player of your alignment is executed, you might be executed instead.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Scapegoat',1,null,1),('Gunslinger','Traveller','Each day, after the 1st vote has been tallied, you may choose a player that voted: they die.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Gunslinger',1,null,1),('Beggar','Traveller','You must use a vote token to vote. If a dead player gives you theirs, you learn their alignment. You are sober and healthy.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Beggar',1,null,1),('Bureaucrat','Traveller','Each night, choose a player (not yourself): their vote counts as 3 votes tomorrow.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Bureaucrat',1,null,1),('Thief','Traveller','Each night, choose a player (not yourself): their vote counts negatively tomorrow.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Thief',1,null,1),('Butcher','Traveller','Each day, after the 1st execution, you may nominate again.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Butcher',1,null,1),('Bone Collector','Traveller','Once per game, at night*, choose a dead player: they regain their ability until dusk.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Bone_Collector',1,null,1),('Harlot','Traveller','Each night*, choose a living player: if they agree, you learn their character, but you both might die.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Harlot',1,null,1),('Barista','Traveller','Each night, until dusk, 2) a player becomes sober, healthy & gets true info, or 2) their ability works twice. They learn which.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Barista',1,null,1),('Deviant','Traveller','If you were funny today, you cannot die by exile.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Deviant',1,null,1),('Apprentice','Traveller','On your 1st night, you gain a Townsfolk ability (if good) or a Minion ability (if evil).','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Apprentice',1,null,1),('Matron','Traveller','Each day, you may choose up to 3 sets of 2 players to swap seats. Players may not leave their seats to talk in private.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Matron',1,null,1),('Voudon','Traveller','Only you & the dead can vote. They don''t need a vote token to do so. A 50% majority isn''t required.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Voudon',1,null,1),('Judge','Traveller','Once per game, if another player nominated, you may choose to force the current execution to pass or fail.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Judge',1,null,1),('Bishop','Traveller','Only the Storyteller can nominate. At least 1 opposing player must be nominated each day.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Bishop',1,null,1),('Gangster','Traveller','Once per day, you may choose to kill an alive neighbor, if your other alive neighbor agrees.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Gangster',1,null,1),('Gnome','Traveller','All players start knowing a player of your alignment. You may choose to kill anyone who nominates them.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Gnome',1,null,1),
('Doomsayer','Fabled','If 4 or more players live, each living player may publicly choose (once per game) that a player of their own alignment dies.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Doomsayer',1,null,1),('Angel','Fabled','Something bad might happen to whoever is most responsible for the death of a new player.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Angel',1,null,1),('Buddhist','Fabled','For the first 2 minutes of each day, veteran players may not talk.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Buddhist',1,null,1),('Hell''s Librarian','Fabled','Something bad might happen to whoever talks when the Storyteller has asked for silence.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Hell''s_Librarian',1,null,1),('Revolutionary','Fabled','2 neighboring players are known to be the same alignment. Once per game, 1 of them registers falsely.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Revolutionary',1,null,1),('Fiddler','Fabled','Once per game, the Demon secretly chooses an opposing player: all players choose which of these 2 players win.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Fiddler',1,null,1),('Toymaker','Fabled','The Demon may choose not to attack & must do this at least once per game. Evil players get normal starting info.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Toymaker',1,null,1),('Fibbin','Fabled','Once per game, 1 good player might get incorrect information.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Fibbin',1,null,1),('Duchess','Fabled','Each day, 3 players may choose to visit you. At night*, each visitor learns how many visitors are evil, but 1 gets false info.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Duchess',1,null,1),('Sentinel','Fabled','There might be 1 extra or 1 fewer Outsider in play.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Sentinel',1,null,1),('Spirit of Ivory','Fabled','There can''t be more than 1 extra evil player.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Spirit_of_Ivory',1,null,1),('Djinn','Fabled','Use the Djinn''s special rule. All players know what it is.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Djinn',1,null,1),('Bootlegger','Fabled','This script has homebrew characters or rules.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Bootlegger',1,null,1),('Ferryman','Fabled','On the final day, all dead players regain their vote token.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Ferryman',1,null,1),('Gardener','Fabled','The Storyteller assigns 1 or more players'' characters.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Gardener',1,null,1),('Storm Catcher','Fabled','Name a good character. If in play, they can only die by execution, but evil players learn which player it is.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Storm_Catcher',1,null,1),
('Washerwoman','Townsfolk','You start knowing that 1 of 2 playrs is a particular Townsfolk.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Washerwoman',1,'niebondźglizdom',1),('Librarian','Townsfolk','You start knowing that 1 of 2 playrs is a particular Outsider, or that zero are in play.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Librarian',1,null,1),('Investigator','Townsfolk','You start knowing that 1 of 2 playrs is playrs particular Minion.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Investigator',1,null,1),('Chef','Townsfolk','You start knowing how many pairs of evil players there are.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Chef',1,null,1),('Empath','Townsfolk','Each night, you learn how many of your 2 alive neighbors are evil.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Empath',1,null,1),('Fortune Teller','Townsfolk','Each night, choose 2 playrs: you learn if either is a Demon. There is a good player that always registers as a Demon to you.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Fortune_Teller',1,null,1),('Undertaker','Townsfolk','Each night*, you learn which character died by execution today.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Undertaker',1,null,1),('Monk','Townsfolk','Each night*, choose a player (not yourself): they are safe from the Demon tonight.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Monk',1,null,1),('Ravenkeeper','Townsfolk','If you die at night, you are woken to choose a player: you learn their character.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Ravenkeeper',1,null,1),('Virgin','Townsfolk','The first time you are nominated, if the nominator is a Townsfolk, they are executed immediately.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Virgin',1,null,1),('Slayer','Townsfolk','Once per game, during the day, publicly choose a player: if they are the Demon, they die.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Slayer',1,null,1),('Soldier','Townsfolk','You are safe from the Demon.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Soldier',1,null,1),('Mayor','Townsfolk','If only 3 playrs live & no execution occurs, your team wins. If you die at night, another player might die instead.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Mayor',1,null,1),('Butler','Outsider','Each night, choose a player (not yourself): tomorrow, you may only vote if they are voting too.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Butler',1,null,1),('Drunk','Outsider','You do not know you are the Drunk. You think you are a Townsfolk character, but you are not.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Drunk',1,null,1),('Recluse','Outsider','You might register as evil & as a Minion or Demon, even if dead.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Recluse',1,null,1),('Saint','Outsider','If you die by execution, your team loses.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Saint',1,null,1),('Poisoner','Minion','Each night, choose a player: they are poisoned tonight and tomorrow day.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Poisoner',1,null,1),('Spy','Minion','Each night, you see the Grimoire. You might register as good & as a Townsfolk or Outsider, even if dead.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Spy',1,null,1),('Baron','Minion','There are 2 extra Outsiders in play.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Baron',1,null,1),('Scarlet Woman','Minion','If there are 5 or more players alive & the Demon dies, you become the Demon. (Travellers don''t count)','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Scarlet_Woman',1,null,1),('Imp','Demon','Each night*, choose a player: they die. If you kill yourself this way, a Minion becomes the Imp.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Imp',1,null,1),('Grandmother','Townsfolk','You start knowing a good player & their character. If the Demon kills them, you die too.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Grandmother',1,null,1),('Sailor','Townsfolk','Each night, choose an alive player: either you or they are drunk until dusk. You can''t die.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Sailor',1,null,1),('Chambermaid','Townsfolk','Each night, choose 2 alive players (not yourself): you learn how many woke tonight  due to their ability.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Chambermaid',1,null,1),('Exorcist','Townsfolk','Each night*, choose a player (different to last night): the Demon, if chosen, learns who you are then doesn''t wake tonight','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Exorcist',1,null,1),('Innkeeper','Townsfolk','Each night*, choose 2 players: they can''t die tonight, but 1 is drunk until dusk.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Innkeeper',1,null,1),('Gambler','Townsfolk','Each night*, choose a player & guess their character: if you guess wrong, you die.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Gambler',1,null,1),('Gossip','Townsfolk','Each day, you may make a public statement. Tonight, if it was true, a player dies.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Gossip',1,null,1),('Courtier','Townsfolk','Once per game, at night, choose a character: they are drunk for 3 nights & 3 days.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Courtier',1,null,1),('Professor','Townsfolk','Once per game, at night*, choose a dead player: if they are a Townsfolk, they are resurrected.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Professor',1,null,1),('Minstrel','Townsfolk','When a Minion dies by execution, all other players (except Travellers) are drunk until dusk tomorrow.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Minstrel',1,null,1),('Tea Lady','Townsfolk','If both your alive neighbors are good, they can''t die.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Tea_Lady',1,null,1),('Pacifist','Townsfolk','Executed good players might not die.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Pacifist',1,null,1),('Fool','Townsfolk','The 1st time you die, you don''t.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Fool',1,null,1),('Goon','Outsider','Each night, the 1st player to choose you with their ability is drunk until dusk. You become their alignment.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Goon',1,null,1),('Lunatic','Outsider','You think you are a Demon, but you are not. The Demon knows who you are & who you choose at night.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Lunatic',1,null,1),('Tinker','Outsider','You might die at any time.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Tinker',1,null,1),('Moonchild','Outsider','When you learn that you died, publicly choose 1 alive player. Tonight, if it was a good player, they die.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Moonchild',1,null,1),('Godfather','Minion','You start knowing which Outsiders are in play. If 1 died today, choose a player tonight: they die. [-1 or +1 Outsider]','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Godfather',1,null,1),('Assassin','Minion','Once per game, at night*, choose a player: they die, even if for some reason they could not.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Assassin',1,null,1),
('Devil''s advocate','Minion','Each night, choose a living player (different to last night): if executed tomorrow, they don''t die.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Devil%27s_Advocate',1,null,1),('Mastermind','Minion','If the Demon dies by execution (ending the game,null), play for 1 more day. If a player is then executed, their team loses.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Mastermind',1,null,1),('Zombuul','Demon','Each night*, if no-one died today, choose a player: they die. The 1st time you die, you live but register as dead.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Zombuul',1,null,1),('Pukka','Demon','Each night, choose a player: they are poisoned. The previously poisoned player dies then becomes healthy.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Pukka',1,null,1),('Shabaloth','Demon','Each night*, choose 2 players: they die. A dead player you chose last night might be regurgitated.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Shabaloth',1,null,1),('Po','Demon','Each night*, you may choose a player: they die. If your last choice was no-one, choose 3 players tonight.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Po',1,null,1),('Clockmaker','Townsfolk','You start knowing how many steps from the Demon to its nearest Minion.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Clockmaker',1,null,1),('Dreamer','Townsfolk','Each night, choose a player (not yourself or Travellers): you learn 1 good & 1 evil character, 1 of which is correct.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Dreamer',1,null,1),('Snake Charmer','Townsfolk','Each night, choose an alive player: a chosen Demon swaps characters & alignments with you & is then poisoned.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Snake_Charmer',1,null,1),('Mathematician','Townsfolk','Each night, you learn how many players'' abilities worked abnormally (since dawn) due to another character''s ability.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Mathematician',1,null,1),('Flowergirl','Townsfolk','Each night*, you learn if a Demon voted today.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Flowergirl',1,null,1),('Town Crier','Townsfolk','Each night*, you learn if a Minion nominated today.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Town_Crier',1,null,1),('Oracle','Townsfolk','Each night*, you learn how many dead players are evil.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Oracle',1,null,1),('Savant','Townsfolk','Each day, you may visit the Storyteller to learn 2 things in private: 1 is true & 1 is false.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Savant',1,null,1),('Seamstress','Townsfolk','Once per game, at night, choose 2 players (not yourself): you learn if they are the same alignment.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Seamstress',1,null,1),('Philosopher','Townsfolk','Once per game, at night, choose a good character: gain that ability. If this character is in play, they are drunk.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Philosopher',1,null,1),('Artist','Townsfolk','Once per game, during the day, privately ask the Storyteller any yes/no question.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Artist',1,null,1),('Juggler','Townsfolk','On your 1st day, publicly guess up to 5 players'' characters. That night, you learn how many you got correct.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Juggler',1,null,1),('Sage','Townsfolk','If the Demon kills you, you learn that it is 1 of 2 players.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Sage',1,null,1),('Mutant','Outsider','If you are \"mad\" about being an Outsider, you might be executed.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Mutant',1,null,1),('Sweetheart','Outsider','When you die, 1 player is drunk from now on.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Sweetheart',1,null,1),('Barber','Outsider','If you died today or tonight, the Demon may choose 2 players (not another Demon) to swap characters.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Barber',1,null,1),('Klutz','Outsider','When you learn that you died, publicly choose 1 alive player: if they are evil, your team loses.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Klutz',1,null,1),('Evil Twin','Minion','You & an opposing player know each other. If the good player is executed, evil wins. Good can''t win if you both live.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Evil_Twin',1,null,1),('Witch','Minion','Each night, choose a player: if they nominate tomorrow, they die. If just 3 players live, you lose this ability.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Witch',1,null,1),('Cerenovus','Minion','Each night, choose a player & a good character: they are \"mad\" they are this character tomorrow, or might be executed.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Cerenovus',1,null,1),('Pit-Hag','Minion','Each night*, choose a player & a character they become (if not in play). If a Demon is made, deaths tonight are arbitrary.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Pit-Hag',1,null,1),('Fang Gu','Demon','Each night*, choose a player: they die. The 1st Outsider this kills becomes an evil Fang Gu & you die instead. [+1 Outsider]','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Fang_Gu',1,null,1),('Vigormortis','Demon','Each night*, choose a player: they die. Minions you kill keep their ability & poison 1 Townsfolk neighbor. [-1 Outsider]','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Vigormortis',1,null,1),('No Dashii','Demon','Each night*, choose a player: they die. Your 2 Townsfolk neighbors are poisoned.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/No_Dashii',1,null,1),('Vortox','Demon','Each night*, choose a player: they die. Townsfolk abilities yield false info. Each day, if no-one is executed, evil wins.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Vortox',1,null,1),('Acrobat','Townsfolk','Each night*, choose a player: if they are or become drunk or poisoned tonight, you die.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Acrobat',1,null,1),('Alchemist','Townsfolk','You have a Minion ability. When using this, the Storyteller may prompt you to choose differently.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Alchemist',1,null,1),('Alsaahir','Townsfolk','Each day, if you publicly guess which players are Minion(s) and which are Demon(s,null), good wins.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Alsaahir',1,null,1),('Amnesiac','Townsfolk','You do not know what your ability is. Each day, privately guess what it is: you learn how accurate you are.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Amnesiac',1,null,1),('Atheist','Townsfolk','The Storyteller can break the game rules, and if executed, good wins, even if you are dead. [No evil characters]','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Atheist',1,null,1),('Balloonist','Townsfolk','Each night, you learn a player of a different character type than last night. [+0 or +1 Outsider]','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Balloonist',1,null,1),
('Banshee','Townsfolk','If the Demon kills you, all players learn this. From now on, you may nominate twice per day and vote twice per nomination.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Banshee',1,null,1),('Bounty Hunter','Townsfolk','You start knowing 1 evil player. If the player you know dies, you learn another evil player tonight. [1 Townsfolk is evil]','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Bounty_Hunter',1,null,1),('Cannibal','Townsfolk','You have the ability of the recently killed executee. If they are evil, you are poisoned until a good player dies by execution.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Cannibal',1,null,1),('Choirboy','Townsfolk','If the Demon kills the King, you learn which player is the Demon. [+the King]','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Choirboy',1,null,1),('Cult Leader','Townsfolk','Each night, you become the alignment of an alive neighbor. If all good players choose to join your cult, your team wins.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Cult_Leader',1,null,1),('Engineer','Townsfolk','Once per game, at night, choose which Minions or which Demon is in play.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Engineer',1,null,1),('Farmer','Townsfolk','When you die at night, an alive good player becomes a Farmer.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Farmer',1,null,1),('Fisherman','Townsfolk','Once per game, during the day, visit the Storyteller for some advice to help your team win.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Fisherman',1,null,1),('General','Townsfolk','Each night, you learn which alignment the Storyteller believes is winning: good, evil, or neither.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/General',1,null,1),('High Priestess','Townsfolk','Each night, learn which player the Storyteller believes you should talk to most.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/High_Priestess',1,null,1),('Huntsman','Townsfolk','Once per game, at night, choose a living player: the Damsel, if chosen, becomes a not-in-play Townsfolk. [+the Damsel]','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Huntsman',1,null,1),('King','Townsfolk','Each night, if the dead equal or outnumber the living, you learn 1 alive character. The Demon knows you are the King.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/King',1,null,1),('Knight','Townsfolk','You start knowing 2 players that are not the Demon.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Knight',1,null,1),('Lycanthrope','Townsfolk','Each night*, choose an alive player. If good, they die & the Demon doesn’t kill tonight. One good player registers as evil.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Lycanthrope',1,null,1),('Magician','Townsfolk','The Demon thinks you are a Minion. Minions think you are a Demon.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Magician',1,null,1),('Nightwatchman','Townsfolk','Once per game, at night, choose a player: they learn you are the Nightwatchman.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Nightwatchman',1,null,1),('Noble','Townsfolk','You start knowing 3 players, 1 and only 1 of which is evil.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Noble',1,null,1),('Pixie','Townsfolk','You start knowing 1 in-play Townsfolk. If you were mad that you were this character, you gain their ability when they die.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Pixie',1,null,1),('Poppy Grower','Townsfolk','Minions & Demons do not know each other. If you die, they learn who each other are that night.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Poppy_Grower',1,null,1),('Preacher','Townsfolk','Each night, choose a player: a Minion, if chosen, learns this. All chosen Minions have no ability.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Preacher',1,null,1),('Shugenja','Townsfolk','You start knowing if your closest evil player is clockwise or anti-clockwise. If equidistant, this info is arbitrary.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Shugenja',1,null,1),('Steward','Townsfolk','You start knowing 1 good player.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Steward',1,null,1),('Village Idiot','Townsfolk','Each night, choose a player: you learn their alignment. [+0 to +2 Village Idiots. 1 of the extras is drunk]','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Village_Idiot',3,null,1),('Damsel','Outsider','All Minions know a Damsel is in play. If a Minion publicly guesses you (once,null), your team loses.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Damsel',1,null,1),('Golem','Outsider','You may only nominate once per game. When you do, if the nominee is not the Demon, they die.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Golem',1,null,1),('Hatter','Outsider','If you died today or tonight, the Minion & Demon players may choose new Minion & Demon characters to be.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Hatter',1,null,1),('Heretic','Outsider','Whoever wins, loses & whoever loses, wins, even if you are dead.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Heretic',1,null,1),('Ogre','Outsider','On your 1st night, choose a player (not yourself): you become their alignment (you don''t know which) even if drunk or poisoned.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Ogre',1,null,1),('Plague Doctor','Outsider','When you die, the Storyteller gains a Minion ability.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Plague_Doctor',1,null,1),('Politician','Outsider','If you were the player most responsible for your team losing, you change alignment & win, even if dead.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Politician',1,null,1),('Puzzlemaster','Outsider','1 player is drunk, even if you die. If you guess (once) who it is, learn the Demon player, but guess wrong & get false info.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Puzzlemaster',1,null,1),('Snitch','Outsider','Each Minion gets 3 bluffs.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Snitch',1,null,1),('Zealot','Outsider','If there are 5 or more players alive, you must vote for every nomination.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Zealot',1,null,1),('Boffin','Minion','The Demon (even if drunk or poisoned) has a not-in-play good character''s ability. You both know which.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Boffin',1,null,1),('Boomdandy','Minion','If you are executed, all but 3 players die. After a 10 to 1 countdown, the player with the most players pointing at them, dies.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Boomdandy',1,null,1),('Fearmonger','Minion','Each night, choose a player: if you nominate & execute them, their team loses. All players know if you choose a new player.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Fearmonger',1,null,1),('Goblin','Minion','If you publicly claim to be the Goblin when nominated & are executed that day, your team wins.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Goblin',1,null,1),('Harpy','Minion','Each night, choose 2 players: tomorrow, the 1st player is mad that the 2nd is evil, or one or both might die.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Harpy',1,null,1),
('Marionette','Minion','You think you are a good character, but you are not. The Demon knows who you are. [You neighbor the Demon]','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Marionette',1,null,1),('Mezepheles','Minion','You start knowing a secret word. The 1st good player to say this word becomes evil that night.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Mezepheles',1,null,1),('Organ Grinder','Minion','All players keep their eyes closed when voting and the vote tally is secret. Each night, choose if you are drunk until dusk.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Organ_Grinder',1,null,1),('Psychopath','Minion','Each day, before nominations, you may publicly choose a player: they die. If executed, you only die if you lose roshambo.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Psychopath',1,null,1),('Summoner','Minion','You get 3 bluffs. On the 3rd night, choose a player: they become an evil Demon of your choice. [No Demon]','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Summoner',1,null,1),('Vizier','Minion','All players know you are the Vizier. You cannot die during the day. If good voted, you may choose to execute immediately.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Vizier',1,null,1),('Widow','Minion','On your first night, look at the Grimoire & choose a player: they are poisoned. 1 good player knows a Widow is in play.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Widow',1,null,1),('Wizard','Minion','Once per game, choose to make a wish. If granted, it might have a price & leave a clue as to its nature.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Wizard',1,null,1),('Xaan','Minion','On night X, all Townsfolk are poisoned until dusk. [X Outsiders]','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Xaan',1,null,1),('Al-Hadikhia','Demon','Each night*, you may choose 3 players (all players learn who): each silently chooses to live or die, but if all live, all die.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Al-Hadikhia',1,null,1),('Kazali','Demon','Each night*, choose a player: they die. [You choose which players are which Minions. -? to +? Outsiders]','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Kazali',1,null,1),('Legion','Demon','Each night*, a player might die. Executions fail if only evil voted. You register as a Minion too. [Most players are Legion]','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Legion',10,null,1),('Leviathan','Demon','If more than 1 good player is executed, evil wins. All players know you are in play. After day 5, evil wins.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Leviathan',1,null,1),('Lil Monsta','Demon','Each night, Minions choose who babysits Lil'' Monsta & ''is the Demon''. Each night*, a player might die. [+1 Minion]','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Lil%27_Monsta',1,null,1),('Lleech','Demon','Each night*, choose a player: they die. You start by choosing a player: they are poisoned. You die if & only if they are dead.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Lleech',1,null,1),('Lord of Typhon','Demon','Each night*, choose a player: they die. [Evil characters are in a line. You are in the middle. +1 Minion. -? to +? Outsiders]','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Lord_of_Typhon',1,null,1),('Ojo','Demon','Each night*, choose a character: they die. If they are not in play, the Storyteller chooses who dies.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Ojo',1,null,1),('Riot','Demon','On day 3, Minions become Riot & nominees die but nominate an alive player immediately. This must happen.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Riot',1,null,1),('Yaggababble','Demon','You start knowing a secret phrase. For each time you said it publicly today, a player might die.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Yaggababble',1,null,1),('Scapegoat','Traveller','If a player of your alignment is executed, you might be executed instead.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Scapegoat',1,null,1),('Gunslinger','Traveller','Each day, after the 1st vote has been tallied, you may choose a player that voted: they die.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Gunslinger',1,null,1),('Beggar','Traveller','You must use a vote token to vote. If a dead player gives you theirs, you learn their alignment. You are sober and healthy.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Beggar',1,null,1),('Bureaucrat','Traveller','Each night, choose a player (not yourself): their vote counts as 3 votes tomorrow.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Bureaucrat',1,null,1),('Thief','Traveller','Each night, choose a player (not yourself): their vote counts negatively tomorrow.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Thief',1,null,1),('Butcher','Traveller','Each day, after the 1st execution, you may nominate again.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Butcher',1,null,1),('Bone Collector','Traveller','Once per game, at night*, choose a dead player: they regain their ability until dusk.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Bone_Collector',1,null,1),('Harlot','Traveller','Each night*, choose a living player: if they agree, you learn their character, but you both might die.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Harlot',1,null,1),('Barista','Traveller','Each night, until dusk, 2) a player becomes sober, healthy & gets true info, or 2) their ability works twice. They learn which.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Barista',1,null,1),('Deviant','Traveller','If you were funny today, you cannot die by exile.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Deviant',1,null,1),('Apprentice','Traveller','On your 1st night, you gain a Townsfolk ability (if good) or a Minion ability (if evil).','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Apprentice',1,null,1),('Matron','Traveller','Each day, you may choose up to 3 sets of 2 players to swap seats. Players may not leave their seats to talk in private.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Matron',1,null,1),('Voudon','Traveller','Only you & the dead can vote. They don''t need a vote token to do so. A 50% majority isn''t required.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Voudon',1,null,1),('Judge','Traveller','Once per game, if another player nominated, you may choose to force the current execution to pass or fail.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Judge',1,null,1),('Bishop','Traveller','Only the Storyteller can nominate. At least 1 opposing player must be nominated each day.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Bishop',1,null,1),('Gangster','Traveller','Once per day, you may choose to kill an alive neighbor, if your other alive neighbor agrees.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Gangster',1,null,1),('Gnome','Traveller','All players start knowing a player of your alignment. You may choose to kill anyone who nominates them.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Gnome',1,null,1),
('Doomsayer','Fabled','If 4 or more players live, each living player may publicly choose (once per game) that a player of their own alignment dies.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Doomsayer',1,null,1),('Angel','Fabled','Something bad might happen to whoever is most responsible for the death of a new player.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Angel',1,null,1),('Buddhist','Fabled','For the first 2 minutes of each day, veteran players may not talk.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Buddhist',1,null,1),('Hell''s Librarian','Fabled','Something bad might happen to whoever talks when the Storyteller has asked for silence.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Hell''s_Librarian',1,null,1),('Revolutionary','Fabled','2 neighboring players are known to be the same alignment. Once per game, 1 of them registers falsely.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Revolutionary',1,null,1),('Fiddler','Fabled','Once per game, the Demon secretly chooses an opposing player: all players choose which of these 2 players win.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Fiddler',1,null,1),('Toymaker','Fabled','The Demon may choose not to attack & must do this at least once per game. Evil players get normal starting info.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Toymaker',1,null,1),('Fibbin','Fabled','Once per game, 1 good player might get incorrect information.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Fibbin',1,null,1),('Duchess','Fabled','Each day, 3 players may choose to visit you. At night*, each visitor learns how many visitors are evil, but 1 gets false info.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Duchess',1,null,1),('Sentinel','Fabled','There might be 1 extra or 1 fewer Outsider in play.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Sentinel',1,null,1),('Spirit of Ivory','Fabled','There can''t be more than 1 extra evil player.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Spirit_of_Ivory',1,null,1),('Djinn','Fabled','Use the Djinn''s special rule. All players know what it is.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Djinn',1,null,1),('Bootlegger','Fabled','This script has homebrew characters or rules.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Bootlegger',1,null,1),('Ferryman','Fabled','On the final day, all dead players regain their vote token.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Ferryman',1,null,1),('Gardener','Fabled','The Storyteller assigns 1 or more players'' characters.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Gardener',1,null,1),('Storm Catcher','Fabled','Name a good character. If in play, they can only die by execution, but evil players learn which player it is.','https://wiki.bloodontheclocktower.com/Storm_Catcher',1,null,1);
